course: dictionary
lesson: 1738
title: Sound words and clang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like what they mean. Clang is one of them: say it out loud and it rings like metal being hit. «The front-door bell clangs, and in bursts the Otter.» The word clangs tells you the bell is loud and metallic, so the reader can almost hear it.
explain: Clang can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it means to make a loud, ringing sound: «The old gaoler's rusty key creaks, the door clangs.» As a noun it is the sound itself: «little balls on threads dropped onto a plate with a clang.» Check which one it is by asking: is something doing the clanging, or is the clang the thing being talked about?
explain: Clang has a second, informal meaning in the UK. To drop a clanger is to make a silly, obvious mistake. Context tells you which meaning is right. If the sentence is about bells, doors or plates, it means the loud sound. If it is about someone getting something wrong, it means a mistake.
fact: Clang means to make a loud, ringing sound like metal being hit.
fact: As a noun, a clang is the loud metal sound itself.
fact: Words like clang are sound words: they sound like the thing they describe.
fact: Similar words include clank, clash and ding, but each has its own feel.
fact: In the UK, informal: «drop a clanger» means to make a silly, obvious mistake.
exercise: «The front-door bell clangs, and in bursts the Otter.» What does clangs mean here? | *A loud, ringing metal sound | A door painted bright red | A soft, gentle whisper | A bird singing in the garden
exercise: Which word is most like clang in sound and meaning? | *Clank | Sparkle | Whisper | Slumber
exercise: Sam says, «I dropped a clanger in the spelling test today.» What does clanger mean here? | A small metal key | A big church bell | *A silly, obvious mistake | A loud metal noise
test: «In China, little balls on threads dropped onto a plate with a clang.» In this sentence, clang is a noun. What does it mean? | To hit something with a hammer | A silly mistake | A plate of food | *The loud metal sound itself
test: Which sentence uses clang as a noun? | *The clang woke the whole house. | Please clang the pans gently. | The bell will clang at noon. | Don't clang the gate shut.
exam: Dad says, «You dropped a clanger, Sam!» What does he mean? | *Sam made a silly, obvious mistake | Sam found a bell in the garden | Sam made a loud noise with a metal tin | Sam is very tall and strong
